    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for August 17 hinges on leveraging favorable matchups against suspect pitching, with **Kyle Tucker** (85.72) standing out as the clear must-start anchor. His elite projection is driven by a massive +14% park factor and a +19% boost from facing the 4.93 xERA of Tomoyuki Sugano. **Andy Pages** (75.63) and **Drake Baldwin** (72.04) represent the next tier of high-value plays; both benefit significantly from weak opposing starters and projected top-of-the-order usage, which maximizes their opportunities for R and RBI. **Jacob Wilson** (61.21) remains a recommended start, as his steady production vs. Michael Wacha provides a solid floor for our middle infield.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical adjustments due to dynamic platoon sensitivities and the scarcity of stolen base threats. **Gunnar Henderson** (53.52) saw his score deflated by a -15% platoon penalty against the southpaw Shane McClanahan, making him a marginal play relative to his usual output. Meanwhile, **Dominic Smith** (58.64) is our most efficient bench-to-start pivot; despite being lower in the order, his +19% SP skill boost against Bailey Ober and a +7% platoon advantage make him a superior option today over deeper roster bench pieces. The most difficult decision involved **Jackson Merrill** (53.86), whose score dipped due to the difficult matchup against Nolan McLean (3.49 xERA). While he maintains a decent efficiency rating, he remains in the lineup primarily because we lack high-upside alternatives to cover our speed requirements. \n\nMonitoring the lineup cards is critical today, as every projected score for **Drake Baldwin**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Coby Mayo**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Dominic Smith**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Liam Hicks** is predicated on these assumed positions. We continue to hold **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** on 